Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:20:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Read the whole story in 2027: keep a late reader's place,
 let any month close (U28 review)

- The reader's place is the day after the furthest day marked read, not the
  first gap: a reader who joins on day 40 and reads on is no longer sent back
  to day 1 (on the page and in My Library).
- The month the day sits in can be closed; it opens again only when the day
  changes.
- One psalm reads "Psalm 51" in the day's list and the month spans, as the
  day's label does, and a psalm's title no longer repeats its reference.
- Context-guide links are 44 px targets.
- "Act Six begins here" rather than "begins today" on a day that may not be
  today; the description and llms.txt say a guide comes where one belongs,
  not on every day.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
